{
  "source": "scripts/color-taylor-script-cut-04.md",
  "wpm": 150,
  "gaps": {
    "line": 0.5,
    "paragraph": 1.2,
    "beat": 2.5
  },
  "lead": 1.8,
  "tail": 3,
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "1.1",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Hey, I'm Taylor.",
      "start": 1.8,
      "end": 3,
      "gapBefore": 1.8
    },
    {
      "id": "1.1",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "I'm a real human.",
      "start": 3.5,
      "end": 5.1,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.2",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "I'm also a user experience and product designer, and I'd like to show you something I've been working on.",
      "start": 5.6,
      "end": 13.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.3",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "It's called Color Taylor.",
      "start": 13.7,
      "end": 15.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.4",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "I'll just move myself out of the way, for now.",
      "start": 15.8,
      "end": 19.8,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.1",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "I've always struggled with mixing colors using RGB.",
      "start": 22.3,
      "end": 25.5,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.1",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "It turned out hue and saturation models were helpful for finding the colors that I want.",
      "start": 26,
      "end": 32.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.2",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Let's say I have this turquoise color, but I want to get to teal, which is darker and more colorful.",
      "start": 32.9,
      "end": 40.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.2",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "How do I dial that into the RGB?",
      "start": 41.4,
      "end": 44.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "I think I need to lower red and blue,",
      "start": 45.1,
      "end": 48.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.4",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "but how much do I change the RGB before the color becomes unfamiliar?",
      "start": 49.2,
      "end": 54.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.5",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Once I understood how hue models and RGB work together, I could more confidently understand how colors were constructed.",
      "start": 54.9,
      "end": 62.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.5",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "That made it easier to choose harmonious colors, which I could then build into larger systems.",
      "start": 63,
      "end": 69.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.6",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "There, that's teal.",
      "start": 69.9,
      "end": 71.1,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.7",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "Our focus for this presentation will be hue, saturation, and brightness.",
      "start": 71.6,
      "end": 76,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.8",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "But the app supports HSL as well, so you can use what's familiar to you.",
      "start": 76.5,
      "end": 82.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.9",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "Color Taylor is meant to be a playground and educational tool for how RGB and HSB work together.",
      "start": 83,
      "end": 90.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.10",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "You see the relationships in real time, to help better understand how colors work on your display.",
      "start": 90.7,
      "end": 97.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.1",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "The color editor on the right should be familiar to most people who have worked with creative tools.",
      "start": 100,
      "end": 107.2,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.2",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "The hexagon on the left is a different way of displaying the same information.",
      "start": 108.4,
      "end": 114,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.3",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Around the hex we have the Hue,",
      "start": 115.2,
      "end": 118,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.4",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "which is an angle that ranges from 0 to 360 degrees.",
      "start": 118.5,
      "end": 122.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.5",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Red is 0...",
      "start": 124.1,
      "end": 125.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.6",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "green is 120...",
      "start": 126.5,
      "end": 127.7,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "and blue is 240.",
      "start": 128.9,
      "end": 130.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.8",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "By laying the primary colors out like this,",
      "start": 131.7,
      "end": 134.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.9",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "we can more easily see how RGB values determine a color's hue.",
      "start": 135.4,
      "end": 140.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "You'll notice, between each of the primary colors we see combinations:",
      "start": 141.4,
      "end": 145.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.11",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "yellow, which is red and green combined;",
      "start": 147,
      "end": 149.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.12",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 12,
      "text": "cyan, which is green and blue;",
      "start": 151,
      "end": 153.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 13,
      "text": "and magenta, which is blue and red.",
      "start": 154.6,
      "end": 157.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.1",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Let's use an orangey color as a reference point,",
      "start": 159.9,
      "end": 163.5,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.2",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Around 30 degrees we'll always have this warm tone between red and yellow.",
      "start": 164.7,
      "end": 169.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.3",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "At the highest saturation and brightness the color will be a combination of",
      "start": 170.4,
      "end": 175.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.4",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "2 parts red,",
      "start": 176.1,
      "end": 177.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.5",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "1 part green,",
      "start": 177.8,
      "end": 179,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.6",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "0 parts blue.",
      "start": 179.5,
      "end": 180.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.1",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Adding saturation increases the range between red, green, and blue.",
      "start": 183.2,
      "end": 187.2,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.2",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Desaturating reduces the range proportionally between these.",
      "start": 188.4,
      "end": 191.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.3",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Saturation scales off the highest value.",
      "start": 192.4,
      "end": 194.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.4",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "In this case Red holds still.",
      "start": 195.3,
      "end": 197.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.5",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Green and blue move toward it or away from it.",
      "start": 198.2,
      "end": 202.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.6",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "When all three are equal, there's no saturation, and you're left with gray.",
      "start": 203.4,
      "end": 208.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.7",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "Notice the hue didn't change, we're still at 30, which is the same orangey source color we started with.",
      "start": 209.8,
      "end": 217.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.8",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "Same hue, only the range between RGB values changed.",
      "start": 217.9,
      "end": 221.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.1",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Brightness is determined by the highest RGB value.",
      "start": 224,
      "end": 227.2,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.2",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "As we adjust the brightness, the hue and saturation are maintained by scaling the RGB values proportionately to each other.",
      "start": 228.4,
      "end": 236.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.3",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Brightness scales off of zero.",
      "start": 237.6,
      "end": 239.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.3",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "All three channels scale together, so the ratios between them stay the same.",
      "start": 240.1,
      "end": 245.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.4",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "At a hundred percent brightness the hex is at its largest,",
      "start": 246.5,
      "end": 250.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.5",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "and lowering it shrinks the size of the hex.",
      "start": 251.4,
      "end": 255,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.6",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Notice we stay at the hue 30 orange while moving brightness.",
      "start": 255.5,
      "end": 259.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.1",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "We'll use the swatches section to show how we can use HSB to set six different variations of the same hue.",
      "start": 262.4,
      "end": 270.8,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.2",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "We can use HSB to come up with a bright desaturated orange, then go down the scale until we have a dark vibrant variant.",
      "start": 272,
      "end": 281.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "7.3",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "This is hinting at what a design system might do.",
      "start": 282.8,
      "end": 286.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "8.1",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "We've been exploring the playground, but if you want the classroom perspective, check out the equations section.",
      "start": 289.3,
      "end": 296.1,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.2",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "It shows the math behind",
      "start": 297.3,
      "end": 299.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "8.3",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "hue,",
      "start": 299.8,
      "end": 300.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.4",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "saturation,",
      "start": 300.7,
      "end": 301.1,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.5",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "brightness,",
      "start": 301.6,
      "end": 302,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.6",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "and HSL conversions,",
      "start": 302.5,
      "end": 303.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.7",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "as well as how Hex and normalized colors are calculated.",
      "start": 304.9,
      "end": 308.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "9.1",
      "beat": 9,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Now we can move on to the demo.",
      "start": 311.4,
      "end": 314.6,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "9.2",
      "beat": 9,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "You can find this demo the first time loading the app,",
      "start": 315.8,
      "end": 320.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "9.3",
      "beat": 9,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "or from the question mark button at the top of the app.",
      "start": 321.4,
      "end": 326.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.1",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Start with the sliders and controls you already know.",
      "start": 328.7,
      "end": 332.3,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "10.2",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Moving one slider will highlight every other slider it affects.",
      "start": 333.5,
      "end": 337.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.3",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Click the droplet button to switch between Source or Mixed colored sliders.",
      "start": 338.7,
      "end": 343.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.4",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Click the tags button to show HTML colors on the hex.",
      "start": 344.7,
      "end": 349.1,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.5",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Drag a handle on the hex and watch the RGB and HSB sliders follow.",
      "start": 350.3,
      "end": 355.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.6",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Have fun exploring and learning about different color models.",
      "start": 357.1,
      "end": 360.7,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.1",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "If you use Figma, I've also made a Color Taylor plugin that you might like to check out.",
      "start": 363.2,
      "end": 370.4,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.2",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "That's Color Taylor!",
      "start": 371.6,
      "end": 372.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.3",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Go play with it, and I hope it helps you see the relationship between RGB and HSB in a different light.",
      "start": 373.3,
      "end": 381.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.4",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "If it's useful, I'd like to hear from you.",
      "start": 382.9,
      "end": 386.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.4",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Questions and feedback are welcome.",
      "start": 387,
      "end": 389,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.5",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Thanks, see ya.",
      "start": 389.5,
      "end": 390.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    }
  ],
